<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Split Sheet Studio Pricing | Free, Creator, and Studio Plans</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Start free with 3 web-only music split sheets monthly, then compare Creator and Studio launch pricing for artists, producers, studios, sync prep, PDFs, and VST3.">
  <link rel="canonical" href="https://splitsheetstudio.com/pricing"><meta name="theme-color" content="#171311">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:title" content="Split Sheet Studio Pricing | Free, Creator, and Studio Plans"><meta property="og:description" content="Compare free, Creator, and Studio launch plans for music split sheets, sync licensing prep, remote signatures, final PDFs, and the Windows VST3 plugin."><meta property="og:url" content="https://splitsheetstudio.com/pricing"><meta property="og:image" content="<%= socialImageUrl %>">
  <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:title" content="Split Sheet Studio Pricing"><meta name="twitter:description" content="Start free, then upgrade to Creator or Studio when your music split sheet volume grows."><meta name="twitter:image" content="<%= socialImageUrl %>">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/premium.css">
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Does Split Sheet Studio have a free plan?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. The Free plan includes 3 completed split sheets per month through the Split Sheet Studio website only. The Windows VST3 plugin and standalone Windows app are paid-plan benefits." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "What is the difference between Creator and Studio?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Creator includes up to 25 completed split sheets per month for artists, producers, and songwriters. Studio includes up to 150 completed split sheets per month for recording studios, engineers, managers, producers, and teams handling repeated sessions." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Does the Free plan require Stripe checkout?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. Free users can create an account with email or Google and start from the website. Stripe checkout is only needed when someone upgrades to Creator or Studio." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Does the Windows VST3 plugin cost extra?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. During launch, the Windows VST3 plugin and standalone Windows app are included with both Creator and Studio paid packages." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Are Split Sheet Studio purchases refundable?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No refunds are offered except where required by law. Users can cancel future subscription renewals through billing support or the Stripe billing portal." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Which DAWs can load the Split Sheet Studio beta?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The current beta is for 64-bit Windows DAWs that support VST3 effects, including Studio One, Ableton Live, FL Studio, Cubase, Nuendo, REAPER, Bitwig Studio, Cakewalk Sonar, Mixcraft, Waveform, Reason, Samplitude, and Adobe Audition." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Do Pro Tools and BandLab load the Split Sheet Studio VST3 beta?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Pro Tools does not natively load VST3 plugins because it requires AAX. BandLab web and mobile tools do not host desktop Windows VST3 plugins, but Cakewalk Sonar on Windows supports VST3 scanning." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How does Split Sheet Studio help artists and producers?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Artists, songwriters, and producers can document song credits, publishing shares, master ownership, contributor details, remote approvals, and final signed PDF records before release day." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How does Split Sheet Studio help recording studios?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Recording studios can close sessions with organized split sheet paperwork, secure signature links, contributor records, and final packets for clients, managers, labels, publishers, and collaborators." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can split sheets help with sync licensing?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "A split sheet does not guarantee a sync placement or clearance, but clean writer, publisher, master, and contributor records can make sync licensing conversations easier to review." } }
    ]
  }
  </script>
</head>
<body class="premium-site"><div class="premium-shell">
  <%- include('partials/site-nav') %>
  <main class="store-page">
    <section class="store-hero premium-container">
      <div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> Launch pricing</div><h1>Start free.<br><span>Upgrade while launch pricing is live.</span></h1><p class="hero-lede">Use the website free for 3 completed split sheets per month. Creator is discounted from $10 to $7/month, and Studio is discounted from $30 to $19/month during launch.</p><div class="compatibility-row"><span>FREE WEB PLAN</span><span>CREATOR <s>$10</s> $7/MO</span><span>STUDIO <s>$30</s> $19/MO</span></div></div>
      <aside class="purchase-card">
        <div class="purchase-label">START ON THE SITE</div><h2>Free web plan</h2><p>Create an account and finish your first split sheets before choosing a paid package.</p><div class="purchase-price"><strong>$0</strong><span>/mo</span></div>
        <a class="premium-button premium-button-primary purchase-button" href="<%= signupUrl %>">Create free account →</a>
        <ul><li>3 completed split sheets/month</li><li>Website workflow only</li><li>Secure remote signature links</li><li>Final PDF delivery included</li></ul>
      </aside>
    </section>
    <% if (typeof error === 'string' && error) { %><div class="premium-container"><div class="premium-alert"><%= error %></div></div><% } %>
    <section class="premium-section premium-container included-section">
      <div class="section-heading pricing-heading">
        <div><div class="section-kicker">Plans</div><h2>Pick the package that matches your session volume.</h2></div>
        <p>Free keeps new users coming back to the website. Creator and Studio unlock higher limits plus the Windows VST3 plugin and standalone Windows app. No separate VST license is required.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pricing-plan-grid">
        <% planOptions.forEach((plan) => { %>
          <% const isFree = plan.key === 'free'; %>
          <article class="pricing-plan-card <%= plan.key === 'studio_pro' ? 'featured-plan' : '' %> <%= isFree ? 'free-plan' : '' %>">
            <div class="plan-card-top">
              <span><%= isFree ? 'Web-only starter' : (plan.key === 'studio_pro' ? 'For higher-volume rooms' : 'For working creators') %></span>
              <% if (plan.key === 'studio_pro') { %><em>Studio favorite</em><% } %>
            </div>
            <h3><%= plan.name %></h3>
            <div class="plan-price-row">
              <% if (plan.compareAtPriceLabel) { %><s><%= plan.compareAtPriceLabel.replace('/mo', '') %></s><% } %>
              <strong><%= plan.priceLabel.replace('/mo', '') %></strong><span>/month</span>
            </div>
            <p class="plan-compact-price"><%= isFree ? 'No Stripe checkout required' : `${plan.discountLabel}: ${plan.compareAtPriceLabel} reduced to ${plan.priceLabel}` %></p>
            <% if (plan.annualPriceLabel) { %><p class="plan-annual"><% if (plan.annualCompareAtPriceLabel) { %><s><%= plan.annualCompareAtPriceLabel %></s> <% } %><%= plan.annualPriceLabel %> annual launch option</p><% } %>
            <p class="plan-description"><%= isFree ? 'For artists and collaborators who want to try the website workflow before making split sheets part of their regular release process.' : plan.description %></p>
            <ul class="plan-feature-list">
              <li><%= plan.monthlySheetLimit %> completed split sheets per month</li>
              <% if (isFree) { %>
                <li>Split Sheet Studio website only</li>
                <li>No VST3 plugin download</li>
                <li>No standalone app download</li>
              <% } else { %>
                <li>Windows VST3 plugin included</li>
                <li>Standalone Windows app included</li>
              <% } %>
              <li>Secure remote signature links</li>
              <li>Final PDF delivery and records</li>
            </ul>
            <% if (isFree) { %>
              <a class="premium-button premium-button-ghost" href="<%= signupUrl %>">Start free</a>
            <% } else { %>
              <a class="premium-button <%= plan.key === 'studio_pro' ? 'premium-button-primary' : 'premium-button-ghost' %>" href="<%= signupUrl %>">Choose <%= plan.name %></a>
            <% } %>
          </article>
        <% }) %>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="premium-section premium-container included-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="section-kicker">Included in the workflow</div><h2>Everything required to move from credits to signatures.</h2></div><p>The plugin uses the same secure hosted account and remote-signing engine as the browser app.</p></div><div class="feature-list-grid"><div><span>01</span><h3>Session capture</h3><p>Song metadata, contributor details, PRO and IPI information, writing and publishing shares.</p></div><div><span>02</span><h3>100% validation</h3><p>Hard percentage rules prevent incomplete composition or master ownership totals.</p></div><div><span>03</span><h3>Remote signing</h3><p>Email secure links to collaborators working in another studio, city, or state.</p></div><div><span>04</span><h3>Final delivery</h3><p>Complete the packet only after every contributor confirms and signs.</p></div></div></section>
    <section class="premium-section requirements-section"><div class="premium-container requirements-grid"><div><div class="section-kicker">System requirements</div><h2>Simple installation. No background app required.</h2></div><ul class="premium-checks"><li><i>✓</i><span>Windows 10 or Windows 11, 64-bit</span></li><li><i>✓</i><span>64-bit Windows DAW with VST3 effect support</span></li><li><i>✓</i><span>Standalone Windows app included</span></li><li><i>✓</i><span>Internet connection for account and delivery workflows</span></li></ul></div></section>
    <section class="premium-section premium-container faq-section"><div class="section-kicker">Music split sheet FAQ</div><h2>Questions artists, producers, and studios ask before checkout.</h2><div class="faq-grid">
      <article><h3>What is included with the Free plan?</h3><p>Free includes 3 completed split sheets per month through the Split Sheet Studio website. It includes the browser workflow, remote signature links, and final PDF delivery, but it does not include the VST3 plugin or standalone app downloads.</p></article>
      <article><h3>What is the difference between Creator and Studio?</h3><p>Creator includes up to 25 completed split sheets per month for artists, producers, and songwriters. Studio raises that to 150 completed split sheets per month for recording studios, engineers, managers, producers, and repeat session teams.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Does the Free plan require Stripe checkout?</h3><p>No. Free users can create an account with email or Google and start from the website. Stripe checkout is only needed when someone upgrades to Creator or Studio.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Does the VST plugin cost extra?</h3><p>No. During launch, the Windows VST3 plugin and standalone Windows app are included with both paid packages. You do not need to buy a separate VST license.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Are there refunds?</h3><p>No refunds are offered except where required by law. You can cancel future subscription renewals through billing support or the Stripe billing portal.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Which DAWs can load the Windows VST3 beta?</h3><p>The beta is built for 64-bit Windows DAWs that support VST3 effects, including Studio One, Ableton Live, FL Studio, Cubase, Nuendo, REAPER, Bitwig Studio, Cakewalk Sonar, Mixcraft, Waveform, Reason, Samplitude, and Adobe Audition.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Do Pro Tools and BandLab support this beta?</h3><p>Pro Tools does not natively load VST3 plugins; it requires AAX. BandLab web and mobile tools do not host desktop Windows VST3 plugins, but Cakewalk Sonar on Windows supports VST3 scanning.</p></article>
      <article><h3>How does this help artists and producers?</h3><p>Artists, songwriters, and producers can document credits, writer shares, publisher shares, master ownership, collaborator emails, remote approvals, and signed final records before the song leaves the session.</p></article>
      <article><h3>How does this help a recording studio?</h3><p>Studios can give clients a repeatable end-of-session paperwork flow: collect ownership details, send secure signature links, track signer status, and deliver a final PDF packet to everyone involved.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Can split sheets help with sync licensing?</h3><p>A split sheet does not guarantee a sync placement or clearance, but organized writer, publisher, master, and contributor records can make sync licensing reviews easier for artists, managers, publishers, labels, and music supervisors.</p></article>
    </div></section>
    <section class="final-cta premium-container"><div class="brand-mark brand-mark-cta" aria-hidden="true"><img class="brand-logo-img" src="/split-sheet-studio-logo.png" width="116" height="116" alt=""></div><h2>Rights clarity belongs in the session.</h2><p>Create your hosted account now, then use the same sign-in inside the plugin.</p><div class="hero-actions centered"><a class="premium-button premium-button-primary" href="<%= signupUrl %>">Create account →</a><a class="premium-button premium-button-ghost" href="<%= appUrl %>">Open web app</a></div></section>
  </main>
  <%- include('partials/site-footer') %>
</div></body></html>
